.TH LIANLI-SESSION 1 "" "Lian Li Linux"
.SH NAME
lianli-session \- provide graphical-session capture for Lian Li desktop displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lianli-session
.RI [ "\-\-login-start" ]
.RI [ "\-\-socket PATH" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The session helper connects the hardware daemon to the active local graphical
session. It supervises a capture worker and manages application-owned virtual
outputs. It must run as the desktop user, not root.
.PP
Native packages arrange graphical-login startup through the user service.
Distrobox requires a host user capture unit entering the intended box; generate
its recipe with
.BR "lianli-control distrobox-service-unit \-\-desktop-session" .
Application binaries stay inside the box.
.PP
System capture verifies the selected host service account against the socket
peer. A Distrobox system daemon uses the host runtime socket and requires the
selected box owner's host and container UID to match.
.PP
The helper is separate from the hardware daemon. Before graphical login,
desktop-mode displays wait for an eligible session; fan, lighting and ordinary
LCD control remain daemon responsibilities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-login-start
Wait for a graphical login and discover its desktop environment before capture.
.TP
.BI "\-\-socket " PATH
Select the daemon IPC socket. The display-channel suffix is added automatically.
.TP
.BI "\-\-service-invocation " ID
Register ownership for the invocation supplied by a host service wrapper.
Use the generated unit rather than inventing invocation IDs.
.TP
.BI "\-\-stop-service " ID
Request termination of only the capture helper registered for that invocation,
with process-identity checks and a bounded exit wait.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The helper uses the active login's XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, WAYLAND_DISPLAY and, on
Hyprland, HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE. Login startup discovers the matching
session environment; do not substitute another user's compositor credentials.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lianli-daemon (1),
.BR lianli-control (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sgtaziz/lian-li-linux/blob/main/docs/distrobox.md
